---
import "../../styles/global.css";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  const project = {
    slug: "multibody-systems",
    title: "Multibody Systems",
    summary: "A general 2D multibody framework that numerically integrates the motion of systems connected by spring-dampers and rigid rods under gravity.",
  };
  return [{ params: { slug: project.slug }, props: { project } }];
}

const { project } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={project.summary} />
    <title>{project.title} — Manuel Delgado Portfolio</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="case-study">
      <header class="case-header"><a href="/Web-Portofolio/#projects">← Projects</a><a href="/Web-Portofolio/">Manuel Delgado Portfolio</a></header>
      <section class="case-hero"><p class="section-index">PROJECT DETAILS</p><h1>Constraint Physics</h1><p>{project.summary}</p></section>
      <article class="constraint-article">
        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT KINEMATICS</p>
          <h2>Geometric compatibility</h2>
          <p>A rigid connection is defined by a holonomic constraint.</p>
          <div class="equation">C(q) = 0</div>
          <p>For the normalized rod used here,</p>
          <div class="equation">C(q) = ‖p<sub>B</sub> − p<sub>A</sub>‖ − L = 0</div>
          <p>If the constraint remains satisfied over time, its velocity- and acceleration-level conditions must also vanish.</p>
          <div class="equation-stack">
            <div class="equation">Jq̇ = 0</div>
            <div class="equation equation-accent">Jq̈ + J̇q̇ = 0</div>
          </div>
          <p>Here, <span class="inline-equation">J = ∂C/∂q</span> is the constraint Jacobian. The acceleration condition keeps the motion compatible with the geometry of the rigid connection.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT FORCES</p>
          <h2>Solving for the reaction force</h2>
          <p>The equations of motion include the constraint force through the Lagrange multiplier λ.</p>
          <div class="equation">Mq̈ = Q<sub>ext</sub> + J<sup>T</sup>λ</div>
          <div class="equation">q̈ = M<sup>−1</sup>Q<sub>ext</sub> + M<sup>−1</sup>J<sup>T</sup>λ</div>
          <p>Substituting this acceleration into the compatibility condition gives</p>
          <div class="equation equation-wide">JM<sup>−1</sup>J<sup>T</sup>λ = −(JM<sup>−1</sup>Q<sub>ext</sub> + J̇q̇).</div>
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section solver-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT SOLVER</p>
          <h2>A linear system at each timestep</h2>
          <div class="solver-definitions">
            <div class="equation">A = JM<sup>−1</sup>J<sup>T</sup></div>
            <div class="equation">b = −(JM<sup>−1</sup>Q<sub>ext</sub> + J̇q̇)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="equation equation-final">Aλ = b</div>
          <p>For the normalized rod constraint, each component of λ has units of force. It represents the axial tension or compression required to maintain the rigid connection.</p>
          <div class="constraint-chain" aria-label="Constraint solver derivation">
            <span>C(q) = 0</span><b>→</b><span>Jq̇ = 0</span><b>→</b><span>Jq̈ + J̇q̇ = 0</span><b>→</b><span>Aλ = b</span>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
